---
description: Generator Server Actions + Route Handlers (Next.js server-side scaffold)
globs:
  - src/app/**/*.ts
  - src/lib/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

Use this rule when creating Server Actions, Route Handlers, or server-side data modules.

GOAL
- Keep server-side logic typed, validated, and consistent with Supabase-first patterns.
- Keep the diff minimal.

SERVER ACTIONS (`src/app/<route>/actions.ts` or colocated)
- Start file with `"use server"` when exporting actions.
- Import Supabase: `import { createClient } from "@/lib/supabase/server"`
- Validate inputs (zod `safeParse` if zod is in project; otherwise explicit guards).
- Return typed result objects `{ data }` or `{ error: string }` — do not throw to client unless intentional.
- Revalidate paths when mutating: `revalidatePath()` / `revalidateTag()` as needed.

ROUTE HANDLERS (`src/app/api/<path>/route.ts`) — use sparingly
- Export named handlers: `GET`, `POST`, etc.
- Use `createClient()` from server for Supabase access.
- Return `NextResponse.json(...)` always — never HTML for API paths.
- Validate query/body before DB calls.

DATA MODULE (`src/lib/<module>.ts`)
- Shared query/mutation functions callable from Server Components and Actions.
- Normalize Supabase types at boundary (BigInt string → number, NUMERIC → number).
- Expose typed functions: `list*`, `get*ById`, `create*`, `update*`, `delete*`.

RPC / PRIVILEGED OPS
- Prefer RPC in `supabase/migrations/**` for multi-table atomic logic.
- Call via `supabase.rpc()` from server-side code only.
- Never expose service-role operations to Client Components.

ANTI-FOOTGUNS
- Do not import `server.ts` createClient in Client Components.
- Do not duplicate auth/session logic outside middleware + Supabase SSR helpers.

VERIFICATION (mandatory after scaffold — Rule 43)
- Run: `npm run lint` + `npm run build`
- Record Target Output + Verification Report in `docs/ai/CHANGE_CHECKLIST.md`
- See `docs/ai/TARGET_OUTPUT_VERIFICATION.md`
